EasyRent Demo Test Flow

Purpose:
This document is for a live end-to-end demo of the EasyRent rental workflow. It is designed to be printed and used as a test checklist during a client walkthrough.


1. Environment Setup
- Ensure Docker is running.
- Start the local PostgreSQL database:
  docker compose up -d db
- Start the frontend app:
  cd frontend
  npm run dev
- Confirm the app is available at:
  http://localhost:3000


2. Account Creation
A. Create a Landlord Account
- Go to /signup
- Select Landlord
- Enter a fresh email, full name, and password
- Submit the form
- Confirm the landlord lands on the dashboard

B. Create a Tenant Account
- Sign out from the landlord account
- Create a new tenant account with a fresh email
- Confirm the tenant lands on the tenant search flow

C. Create a Handyman Account
- Sign out again
- Create a new handyman account
- Enter services offered, experience, and certifications if applicable
- Confirm the handyman lands on the handyman provider dashboard


3. Landlord Property Listing
- Sign in as the landlord
- Open the dashboard
- Click Create Listing / List Your Property
- Enter:
  - title
  - address
  - monthly rent
  - bedrooms/bathrooms/size
  - description
  - property type
- Upload at least one property image
- Click Publish Listing
- Confirm the listing appears in the landlord dashboard and in the property search flow

Acceptance Criteria:
- Listing is visible to the tenant
- At least one uploaded image is visible on preview/search


4. Tenant Property Search and Application
- Sign in as the tenant
- Open /find-home or property listing page
- Search for the property
- Open the property details
- Click Apply
- Complete the application form
- Submit the application

Acceptance Criteria:
- Application is created successfully
- Tenant sees confirmation status


5. Landlord Application Review
- Sign in as the landlord
- Open the dashboard or applications view
- Review the new application
- Approve or review the applicant

Acceptance Criteria:
- Application status changes to approved or reviewed
- Landlord can view applicant information


6. Payment Flow
- Sign in as the tenant
- Open the application or payment step
- Complete the payment/checkout process using the sandbox payment flow
- Confirm payment status updates successfully

Acceptance Criteria:
- Payment page loads correctly
- Payment is successfully processed in sandbox mode
- Invoice / payment status reflects success


7. Maintenance / Repair Request Flow
- Sign in as the tenant
- Submit a repair request or maintenance issue
- Confirm the request is created
- Sign in as the landlord
- Open maintenance requests
- Assign an available handyman
- Sign in as the handyman
- View assigned work request
- Confirm the handyman dashboard shows the provider information and assigned work

Acceptance Criteria:
- Maintenance request is visible to landlord and handyman
- Handyman can see assigned jobs
- Assignment flow works end to end


8. Final Demo Checklist
- Fresh accounts created without seeded demo data
- Landlord listing published with image preview
- Tenant submits application
- Landlord approves application
- Payment completes in sandbox mode
- Repair request created and assigned
- Handyman sees role-specific dashboard
- No fake overdue or demo data remains visible


9. Demo Summary Script
"We created a real landlord, tenant, and handyman account using the live app. The landlord listed a property, uploaded a real image, and published it. The tenant applied, the landlord reviewed and approved the application, and the tenant completed the sandbox payment. We then logged a maintenance request, assigned the handyman, and confirmed the service provider flow."


10. Signoff
